      "dom_id": "question-52230",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that ${p}^{2}-4p+4=0,$ what are the values of $p?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the left-hand side is a perfect square. It just needs to be factored:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{2}-4p+4 & =0 \\\\ {p}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot p+{2}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (p-2)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(p-2)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{0} \\\\ |p-2| & =0 \\\\ p-2 & =0 \\\\ p & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
